---
source: crates/agentgateway/src/import/litellm.rs
description: src/tests/import/litellm/db-state-team-lifetime-pool-no-window.yaml
---
source: litellm
config:
  config:
    database:
      url: "sqlite://data.db"
  gateways:
    default:
      port: 4000
  ui:
    gateways: default
  llm:
    gateways: default
    models:
      - name: chat
        provider: openAI
        params:
          model: gpt-4o
    policies:
      apiKey:
        keys:
          - key: $LITELLM_MASTER_KEY
            metadata:
              name: master
          - keyHash: "sha256:eeee5555eeee5555eeee5555eeee5555eeee5555eeee5555eeee5555eeee5555"
            metadata:
              name: daily
            budgets:
              - name: litellm
                limit:
                  unit: USD
                  amount: 100
                onBudgetExceeded: Block
        mode: strict
findings:
  - sourcePath: "model_list[0]"
    status: exact
    message: Imported model deployment for chat
  - sourcePath: general_settings.master_key
    status: approximate
    message: "Mapped LiteLLM's master_key (an admin-equivalent credential, not a per-user virtual key) to strict Authorization Bearer authentication; LiteLLM also accepts other credential headers. Per-user virtual-key migration needs LiteLLM's database state, not config.yaml alone."
  - sourcePath: "db_state.teams[team-1]"
    status: approximate
    message: "Split team \"team-1\"'s remaining budget pool ($100.00) equally across 1 key(s) with no budget of their own ($100.00 each); agentgateway has no team construct, so this is a one-time snapshot, not a live shared pool"
  - sourcePath: "db_state.keys[0]"
    status: manual
    message: "Key has a LiteLLM budget_duration (\"1d\"), but its migrated amount is a one-time snapshot of a team budget pool share, not a standalone per-key allowance; a recurring window on a fixed pool share would hand the key that share again every period, so no window was applied - review whether the team itself needs its own budget handling"
  - sourcePath: "db_state.keys[0]"
    status: exact
    message: "Migrated key \"daily\" to llm.policies.apiKey (hash-based, no plaintext)"
